# Minimal Module Surface

Prefer private helpers and narrow public APIs. The audits found many exports that were only used in their own file, only re-exported from barrels, or kept alive by tests.

## Rules

- Do not export a symbol unless another production module imports it or it is a deliberate public API for the feature.
- Keep file-local helpers, constants, types, and small components unexported by default.
- Do not add barrel exports speculatively. Add to an `index.ts` only when there is an actual consumer or a clear public feature API.
- Do not keep production exports solely so tests can import internals. Test public behavior, or move pure logic to a deliberately exported utility.
- For service modules with an exported object API, avoid also exporting every implementation function unless direct named imports are intended.
- Remove deprecated props/aliases instead of preserving unused compatibility inside app-local components.

## Cleanup Check

When touching a module, quickly check whether new or existing exports are consumed outside the file. If not, make them private unless there is a documented reason.
